{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows dopamine hydrochloride on shortage since 2017-11-06 with Baxter, Hikma, and Hospira listed as current; our three sites each have about 12–14 days on hand and the preferred alternate is HF Acquisition Co LLC, DBA HealthFirst, which is not on FDA's shortage list today but its label names no plant we could place.",
  "headline_cites": ["E22", "E19", "E20", "E21", "D1", "D2", "D3", "D6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the dopamine hydrochloride shortage on 2017-11-06 and as of 2026-10-21 it has been on the list for 108 months.",
      "cites": ["E22", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The current FDA shortage list includes Baxter Healthcare, Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc., and Hospira Inc. (a Pfizer Company) all with status Current.",
      "cites": ["E19", "E20", "E21"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hikma's label names HIKMA FARMACÊUTICA (PORTUGAL) as the manufacturing plant, but the plant is not placed in our records.",
      "cites": ["E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira's registered plant (FEI 1021343) has a history of OAI inspections in 2010 and 2011 and a Warning Letter in 2010-04-12, with the most recent inspection NAI on 2025-02-07.",
      "cites": ["E8", "E10", "E12", "E17", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East, Corvale General, and Corvale Lakeside each hold roughly 12–14 days of supply at current usage rates.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑selected alternate manufacturer is HF Acquisition Co LLC, DBA HealthFirst, which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Buyer should verify HealthFirst's supply reliability and confirm the manufacturing site before committing to purchase.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    }
  ]
}
